    "metadata": {
      "title": "exchange interactions derived from fitting inelastic neutron scattering",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17160565",
      "publication_date": "2025-09-19",
      "description": "<p>The data contains details of exchange interactions derived from fitting inelastic neutron scattering (INS) data to spin-wave (SW) theory for over 70 magnetic compounds. Additionally, Monte Carlo simulation data for each compound, generated using <a href=\"https://github.com/nafiserb/ESpinS\">ESpinS</a>, is included.<br><br></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The data is also available on GitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/malaei/Magnetic_data/tree/main/INS_SW_MC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://github.com/malaei/Magnetic_data/tree/main/INS_SW_MC</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you use this dataset, please cite:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mojtaba Alaei, Zahra Mosleh, Nafise Rezaei, Artem R. Oganov,<br><em>From Spin Waves to Monte Carlo Simulations: Compiling an Experimental Exchange Interaction Dataset for Magnetic Materials</em>,<br><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2504.15764\" rel=\"nofollow\">arXiv:2504.15764</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
      "access_right": "open",
